“Inspired by MAST, we joint model the proportion of dropouts and the gene expressions of non-dropouts by a two-component mixture model.” (Ji et al., 2022, p. 2)
\par
“empirically that the lognormal distribution works best for most of the data that we explored.” (Ji et al., 2022, p. 2)
\par
“The weights can be either learned from training data with at most one rare cell population, or pre-specified as equal weights on the training data with at least two rare cell populations.” (Ji et al., 2022, p. 2)
\par
“we defined a rare cell population as a cell population with less than 100 cells in a given dataset” (Ji et al., 2022, p. 2)
\par
“scAnnotate removes batch effects using the Seurat package (Hao et al., 2021) for data with at most one rare cell population or the Harmony package (Korsunsky et al., 2018) for data with at least two rare cell populations.” (Ji et al., 2022, p. 3)
